Usage: agent-deck session fork <id|title> [options]

Fork a Claude, OpenCode, Pi, Codex, or Oh My Pi session with conversation context.

Options:
  -b	Create new branch/bookmark (use with --worktree)
  -g string
    	Group for forked session (short)
  -group string
    	Group for forked session
  -json
    	Output as JSON
  -new-branch
    	Create new branch/bookmark
  -q	Minimal output (short)
  -quiet
    	Minimal output
  -sandbox
    	Run forked session in Docker sandbox
  -sandbox-image string
    	Docker image for sandbox (overrides config default)
  -t string
    	Title for forked session (short)
  -title string
    	Title for forked session
  -w string
    	Create fork in a worktree/workspace for branch (git or jj)
  -with-state
    	Carry parent's uncommitted working state into the new worktree/workspace (git or jj; #1029/#1305, requires -w)
  -with-state-and-gitignored
    	Like --with-state, plus gitignored files (e.g. .env). Implies --with-state. Requires -w.
  -worktree string
    	Create fork in a worktree/workspace for branch (git or jj)

Examples:
  agent-deck session fork my-project
  agent-deck session fork my-project -t "my-fork"
  agent-deck session fork my-project -t "my-fork" -g "experiments"
  agent-deck session fork my-project -w fork/experiment
  agent-deck session fork my-project -w fork/new-idea -b
  agent-deck session fork my-project -w fork/wip -b --with-state
  agent-deck session fork my-project -w fork/wip -b --with-state-and-gitignored
